From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PowerPhone Build <powerphone@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 4 Sep 2026 07:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tinyalsa: honor an explicit PCM avail-min

The public pcm_config carries an avail_min override, but the v2 RW setup
always replaced it with one complete period. Honor a nonzero caller value
while preserving the period-sized default for every existing zero-valued
configuration.
---
diff --git a/src/pcm.c b/src/pcm.c
index de22098..399e90a 100644
--- a/src/pcm.c
+++ b/src/pcm.c
@@ -507,7 +507,11 @@ int pcm_set_config(struct pcm *pcm, const struct pcm_config *config)
     memset(&sparams, 0, sizeof(sparams));
     sparams.tstamp_mode = SNDRV_PCM_TSTAMP_ENABLE;
     sparams.period_step = 1;
-    sparams.avail_min = config->period_size;
+    /* Honor the public override.  PowerPhone uses the legacy tinyalsa RW
+     * value of one frame; retain tinyalsa v2's period-sized default for every
+     * caller that leaves this field zero. */
+    pcm->config.avail_min = sparams.avail_min =
+        config->avail_min ? config->avail_min : config->period_size;
 
     if (!config->start_threshold) {
         if (pcm->flags & PCM_IN)
-- 
